record.statement:
For every integer $\[1m\ell\[0m$, there exists $C_\ell>0$ such that, if a graph $G$ contains none of the following as an induced subgraph:

- a subdivision of an $\ell\times\ell$ wall;
- the line graph of a subdivision of an $\ell\times\ell$ wall;
- $K_{\ell,\ell}$;
- $K_\ell$;

then $\operatorname{treewidth}(G)\le C_\ell\log |V(G)|$.
